Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)
1. Do I need an account to use the app?
If you are only browsing for items or looking to buy, you do not need to create a seller profile. However, because NotGumtree securely syncs with your Apple ID, you must be signed into iCloud on your device to use the app. To list an item for sale, you must create a Seller Profile.

2. Why was my email address rejected when creating a Seller Profile?
To protect our community from spam and scams, NotGumtree verifies all seller email addresses. We do not accept temporary, disposable, or invalid email addresses. Please ensure you are using a legitimate, active email address (like Gmail, Outlook, Yahoo, etc.).

3. How do I contact a seller?
When you find an item you are interested in, tap on it to view the details. At the bottom of the screen, tap the "Contact Seller" button. This will reveal the seller's verified phone number and email address so you can reach out to them directly.

4. How do I report a suspicious listing or an abusive user?
Keeping NotGumtree safe is our top priority:

To Report a Listing: Open the item's detail page, scroll to the bottom, and tap "Report this listing." The item will be immediately hidden and sent to our moderation team for review.

To Block a User: Tap "Contact Seller" on any listing, and select "Block User." You will no longer see items posted by this seller.

5. How do I delete my listings or my account?

Delete an item: Go to your Seller Dashboard, find the active advert, and tap "Delete Advert." It will be permanently removed from the marketplace.

Delete your account: To completely remove your seller profile and all associated data, please contact our support team using the email below. We process all data deletion requests within 30 days.

6. Why aren't my photos uploading?
You can upload a maximum of 10 photos per listing. Please ensure you have a stable internet connection. The app will automatically optimize and compress your photos for you, but very large panoramas or unsupported image formats may occasionally fail.

